Z||000000||BroCar 87||06-15-2000||12:35 PM||||Yesterday I was in Wal-mart, and I saw a Pontiac magazine. At the top it had "Headers FOR ANY Pontiac". So I opened it up to see what company's carried headers for my lil 87 4 cyl.  I didn't see any, BUT Hooker headers had them for the 84-86 151 (4 cyl.). Are the 84-86 (4 cyl) different from the 87 4 cyl. Would it be worth it to get headers... if it was a reasonable price? <BR>Thanks for reading and any replies too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||87ECO5||06-15-2000||12:58 PM||||From what I've heard, the Duke will benefit from the better flowing unit, but it's designed in such a way that, unless you protect your starter with a heat shield, you'll be replacing the starter regularly.<P>I've been looking at the heat-treated exhaust manifold from The Fiero Store.  According to them, it's built for the '84-'86 4-bangers but can be fitted to the '87-'88 engines by use of a special flange.  The same may be true for the header.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||06-15-2000||01:28 PM||||A special Flange??? is that at the bottom of the header (or manifold) where it connects to the rest of the exhaust, or where it bolts up to the engine? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||BroCar 87||06-15-2000||07:09 PM||||Ahhh  I went to the fiero store web site and saw what you were talking about. <P>On racesearch.com they have the hooker headers for:<P>#4702: $275  retail: $325<BR>#4703: $290  retail: $345<BR>and also they have the metallic creamic coated    #4703-1 $525  retail  $621 <P><BR>WOW  these are pretty expen$ive huh! <BR>Makes me think... Which am I better off to get, Ported Manifold with the coating or a header.    <BR>what do you guys think??||||reg||1
Z||000004||ggarsk||06-15-2000||08:29 PM||||you can get A Hooker #4702 from summit racing for $265 plus shipping and another $53 for the reducer with the O2 sensor hole. It takes about 3 weeks(special order) I just got mine and I'm putting it on next weekend ,with a Holley 300 and Edelbrock performer manifold.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||06-16-2000||01:58 AM||||Had a Hooker Tri Y Super Competition header for my 87 coupe. No special flanges were needed but the bottom of the tri Y is very close to the starter. FANTASTIC flow though. Just need to look at the exhaust side by side to see the difference. Best thing I ever did to the Duke! ||||reg||14
